Well, this post won't be to long because i lost my notes. Mainly, i am
going to breeze through it. (and i think i got some of my facts mixes
up, so ..)

Crazy the gnomish Healer started life with 2 blessed !oEH. I drank
those and the healing potions and i think i saved the other two. Yes,
i was doing the racket. 



My first stop was sokobon but i took a quick peek into the mines.  For
some reason this quick peek turned into a full dive into mine town
and i ended up donating for about 6 points of protection.  What i
think happened was that i found a bones file of a wizard and i use
the wands of digging to get me to minetown at exp level 1. I didn't
stay long because i wanted Huxtable, my pet dog, not to get killed by
the watch captain. 

Back to the main branch and i tamed an extra kitten and found a fair
size lepy hall on dlvl 6. I left it alone. I don't remember if i
found any shops before then. The oracle was all the way down on dlvl
9. I did manage to find a free altar so was able to get holy water
and get 20 more hp from drinking 4 blessed !oEH. 

On level 8 there was a giant zoo and On level 10 i found the entrance
to sokobon. Before i could enter i dipped below to 11 and found a
huge lepy hall and when i went back up i hit a trap door that dropped
me on a level with a throne room or zoo.  I had to write Elbereth and
sleep some monsters to get back up since i woke them up. Somehow i
made it without having to kill anything. 

I don't remember what sokobon gave me but i do know that i had
reflection, a BoH and MR  so i knew i was going to win already, but i
wasn't sure how long to was going to take. In sokobon i found a wand
o poly and got a blue dragon and i think an olag-hai. Whatever it was
it could take out a lep in one or two hits. This is where the real
fun began. 

I cleared every shop lep hall, throne room and zoo with my pets.
Because my pets killed of l's before they could take any action i
also got more !ofGl , EH,  and FH than i normally would. I upped my
HP even more.  In the end had more money than i usually have for the
racket. 

Next stop, minetown. When i arrived i let my pets take care of the
shop keepers and was able to donate for about naked ac of -5.  Then 
we ate the priest and converted the altar. I was crowned and received 
vorpal blade.  . I just stayed long enough to max my luck since i
really find sac fests a boring part of the game. 

I just breezed through the rest of the game but i found about 2 or
three temples before i even reached the valley. I think my naked ac
reached about -8. Once i got the staff i ditched my pets and just
started slaughtering things left and right. I did find a sink and
altar on the same level so i did some pudding farming for spellbooks.
I didn't do that long because sacing really does bore me to tears. 


Jump to the sanctum.  I wanted to try out the new trick i read about
recently on the newsgroup with going down into the sanctum, coming
back up and level porting into what will hopefully be the middle
room. The drinking a cursed!ofGL on the way back up. 

I don't come up with to many tricks anymore because the tdttoe. Last
trick i tried was to use the portal into the wizard tower for a short
cut, but when i got to the last lvl I drank a  cursed !ogl and it
didn't work! Then i dropped the amulet and tried to teleport it out.
No dice. I didn't have a pet or i would have tried to magic whistled
him out of the tower. I guess i'll try that next game. I also could
have waited for rodney or some demon lord but didn't want to wait. 

This game i went down, came back up, and read a cursed ?ot. I did it
twice before i found myself in the middle room. Killed the high
priest and curses, i drank all my potions of gain level. I had
charmed an Archon on the way down so what i did next was to let him
pick up the amulet and lvl ported myself up one level. Then i came
down and magic whistled him to me. I crossed my fingers and zapped
probing at him. YES, YES, YES! In your face dev team. 

After some practice with the staff i found this to be a really good
weapon. Most things are not lvl drain resistant and the things that
are usually fall quick enough in melee. The only exception would be
liches and demon lords, but they respect elbereth. Anyways, i
genocided all L's so i did not see many of those critters. 

The planes were a snap with two pet archons, but i lost them on the
plane of water. Something died or was generated on the portal so i
did not see it at all before stumbling into it. It  Happened like
that in my last three games. 

Astral was a snap. I stuffed myself until sat and went up the middle.
(I always go up the middle first.) I put on a blind fold to see which
rider i was going to get and it turned out to be death. So i just
powered through with melee into the temple. It was the N one so...

